{"artifact_id":"extract_203e6fb8f7b293c0c1439082","byte_end":69015,"byte_start":66770,"format_id":"reviewed-html-paragraph-v1","locator":"Ch0.S3.p9.2","original_html":"<p id=\"Ch0.S3.p9.2\" class=\"ltx_p\">where <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p9.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"m_{\\PW}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext class=\"undefined\">\\PW</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m_{\\PW}</annotation></semantics></math> is the mass of the <span id=\"Ch0.S3.p9.2.1\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\PW</span> boson, <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p9.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\hat{s}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\hat{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is the square of the partonic center-of-mass energy, and <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p9.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\Theta\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">\u0398</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> is the Heaviside step function. The partonic cross section is parameterized by the two parameters <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p9.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"E_{\\text{sph}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>sph</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{\\text{sph}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p9.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"p_{\\text{sph}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>sph</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p_{\\text{sph}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the latter is a dimensionless phenomenological pre-exponential factor that scales the reference sphaleron production cross section above the threshold <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p9.m6\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"E_{\\text{sph}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>sph</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E_{\\text{sph}}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThe sphaleron samples were generated assuming <math id=\"Ch0.S3.p9.m7\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"p_{\\text{sph}}=1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>sph</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p_{\\text{sph}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, which facilitates setting a limit on this factor.</p>","parser_version":"1.0.0","purpose":"RESEARCH","review_status":"PROPOSED","schema_version":"1.0.0","source_hash":"7fadcfce5fce60055ccd817d98d05c9d09e4c759f1691022a0d3f4f7cf2be955","source_id":"cms_paper_v2","source_version":"2604.10732v2"}